                                "example_id": "07079cab-5551-4b1b-b165-6755f8453389",
                                "sense_id": "806cd3fe-d464-3af9-9e7c-dbbcac5d18db",
                                "text": "For the ground, that means using three primary types of equipment:\n■ Extensometers to look for ground heave - the upwards movement of soil, which can occur at any stage. It is essentially the opposite of erosion and is often associated with clay-type soils which swell when wet.\n■ Inclinometers, which measure slope movements.\n■ Piezometers to measure water levels."
                            }
